      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Sentry is a security software framework that monitors AI agents and enforces policies governing their access to models, tools, and data.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/inside-nvidia-sentry-secure-ai-agents-at-runtime/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T09:52:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:17.695Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Part of the NVIDIA OpenShell reference architecture announced at GTC Berlin, it’s built on NVIDIA DOCA , runs on NVIDIA BlueField-4 DPUs , and provides host-isolated runtime protection for AI agents.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/inside-nvidia-sentry-secure-ai-agents-at-runtime/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T09:52:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:17.695Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In addition to inspecting agent communications, NVIDIA Sentry uses out-of-band observability to establish real-time situational awareness, continuously evaluating agents’ runtime security and behavior to validate their security and integrity.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/inside-nvidia-sentry-secure-ai-agents-at-runtime/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T09:52:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:17.695Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Sentry builds on that foundation to continuously monitor AI agent behavior and enforce access policies independently of host software, establishing a strict security boundary in a separate hardware trust domain outside the agent’s reach to keep agents operating within t…",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/inside-nvidia-sentry-secure-ai-agents-at-runtime/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T09:52:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:17.695Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA OpenShell is a secure runtime for autonomous agents that governs what an agent can do.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/inside-nvidia-sentry-secure-ai-agents-at-runtime/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T09:52:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:17.695Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Sentry adds an independent hardware safeguard out of band, running on BlueField-4, beyond the agent’s reach and knowledge.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/inside-nvidia-sentry-secure-ai-agents-at-runtime/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T09:52:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:17.695Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Sentry can contain and quarantine agents within milliseconds using BlueField-4 in-silicon enforcement capabilities without the cooperation of the agent or the host software.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/inside-nvidia-sentry-secure-ai-agents-at-runtime/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T09:52:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-22T00:39:17.695Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Sentry brings that control into an independent infrastructure domain, combining application-layer inspection through DOCA Tower with runtime evidence and visibility from DOCA Argus and in-silicon enforcement on BlueField-4.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/inside-nvidia-sentry-secure-ai-agents-at-runtime/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T09:52:16.000Z",
